From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:53:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Don't call getrusage() in NtDelayExecution().

Only a zero timeout returned the NtYieldExecution() status, and
Windows may return STATUS_SUCCESS there too. Yield directly and keep
the getrusage() pair in NtYieldExecution().

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
index 67ab945..fed63c0 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
@@ -2483,10 +2483,10 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtDelayExecution( BOOLEAN alertable, const LARGE_INTEGER *timeou
             when = now.QuadPart - when;
         }
 
-        /* Note that we yield after establishing the desired timeout, but
-           we only care about the result of the yield for zero timeouts */
-        status = NtYieldExecution();
-        if (!when) return status;
+#ifdef HAVE_SCHED_YIELD
+        sched_yield();
+#endif
+        if (!when) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 
         for (;;)
         {
